 "drug_rule": "Doxepin is a tricyclic antidepressant that inhibits serotonin reuptake and has significant anticholinergic activity. Quetiapine is an atypical antipsychotic with moderate serotonergic and anticholinergic properties. Co-administration can lead to additive serotonergic excess (risk of serotonin syndrome) and synergistic anticholinergic effects (risk of severe CNS depression, confusion, and orthostatic hypotension). In bipolar II, antidepressant monotherapy without mood stabilizer co-therapy increases the risk of rapid cycling and manic switch.",
